{
  "schema": "style-preset/1",
  "id": "night-case-file",
  "label": "Night Case File",
  "description": "A true story documentary at night. Dark blue-black scenes, faceless figures glowing in one color, rooms and streets built from simple shapes, date and place stamps, an evidence board. Nothing violent is ever shown: a light flashes and a sound is heard. Scripts are fact-checked, and the sources go into the Publishing Card.",
  "engine": "script",
  "factChecked": true,
  "scriptNote": "A true story told in the order it happened, using only facts the research supports. Say the date and the place of each event, and the key numbers in digits. Write sentences of 8 to 16 words, one fact per sentence, because each one gets its own shot. Never describe a weapon, blood or how anyone was hurt: say only that something happened, and move on. Call people by their role, and never describe a real person's looks. If a fact is uncertain, say that it is.",
  "ideaNote": "Each video tells one true story, a documented case or event, in the order it happened, with its dates and places.",
  "defaults": {
    "broll": false,
    "research": true,
    "mood": "dark"
  },
